<title>UK: Pace chief to go when successor found-paper.</title>
<headline>Pace chief to go when successor found-paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pace Micro Technology Plc chief executive David Hood will stand down when a replacement is found after the group issued two profit warnings in the space of a month, the Financial Times reported on Monday.</p>
<p>With Hood's co-chief executive Barry Rubery having already departed, investors met chairman Peter Morgan last week and pressed the company to appoint a single chief with public company experience, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
